{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Abraham, Abraham.</b> An expression of endearment. And the reason He did not call him with a double expression of endearment the first time is that his endearment was not yet made known to all who come into the world, for perhaps he would not withstand the trial. But after he withstood the trial, then it became visible to the eyes of all with surpassing exaltation and surpassing strength over all others; therefore He called him 'Abraham, Abraham' — twice — an expression of endearment, for this trial was for the benefit of the one tested, to make known his endearment." "Another matter: because at the time he was occupied with the commandment of binding his son, he was so entirely absorbed in the commandment to complete it according to its proper procedure, that he would not have paid attention to the voice of the call — therefore it was necessary to call him a second time. And this is the reason for doubling 'Abraham, Abraham,' unlike the first time (Genesis 12:1) when he was not yet absorbed in a commandment. And some say that Abraham understood from this call that they would restrain him from on high; therefore he made himself as one stunned and as a man who does not hear, in order to complete the commandment, until He called him a second time."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:06.044369975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}